cing="multiple:1.15" textAlign="left" wrap="false"><p>exact_vs_atg Ridge positive (Δρ +0.358460); trunc_d0_vs_simple mixed. Clean upstream/start decomposition deferred to RK34.</p></content></shape><shape width="780" height="13" topLeftX="48" topLeftY="512" type="text"><content verticalAlign="top" fontSize="8.2" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(100, 116, 139, 1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.15" textAlign="left" wrap="false"><p>Source: result c811bb6e3481 · primary seed 20261221 · null intercept ρ −0.367234 / MSE 0.194471</p></content></shape><shape width="62" height="15" topLeftX="850" topLeftY="510" type="text"><content verticalAlign="top" fontSize="10" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(31, 41, 55, 1)" bold="true" lineSpacing="multiple:1.15" textAlign="right" wrap="false"><p>168</p></content></shape></data><note><content><p>On the primary seed, exact local context is strongest (Ridge ρ 0.666, HistGB ρ 0.705); the natural truncated window keeps most of that gain.</p><p>The CDS-start and dangles-0 arms sit between simple and exact, consistent with a coverage gradient rather than a single necessary element.</p><p>Secondary contrasts are descriptive only because the body shifts; the clean upstream-versus-start decomposition is left to RK34.</p></content></note></slide>
